<article class="env-lemma" id="0BV5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BV5">Lemma <span data-tag="0BV5">48.21.3</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0F42" data-tag="0F42">48.16.1</a> let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of $\textit{FTS}_ S$. Let $x \in X$ with image $y \in Y$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  H^ i(f^!\mathcal{O}_ Y)_ x \not= 0 \Rightarrow - \dim _ x(X_ y) \leq i.  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since the statement is local on $X$ we may assume $X$ and $Y$ are affine schemes. Write $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ and $Y = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$. Then $f^!\mathcal{O}_ Y$ corresponds to the relative dualizing complex $\omega _{A/R}^\bullet $ of Dualizing Complexes, Section <a href="/tag/0E9M" data-tag="0E9M">47.25</a> by Remark <a href="/tag/0BV2" data-tag="0BV2">48.17.5</a>. Thus the lemma follows from Dualizing Complexes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0E9P" data-tag="0E9P">47.25.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>